@*
    The Prompts tab's content: every model-facing prompt, grouped and editable. The parent
    (Settings.razor) owns all state - this component holds none of its own, the same split
    Teammates.razor uses with TeammateCard: Groups already carries each field's pending value,
    computed flags and validation Issues, and every edit or reset request is handed back to the
    parent through a callback rather than written here.

    Every [Parameter] below is deliberately non-string (PromptEdit for the edited value, plain string
    only for ResetRequested's key - see the note there) for the same reason TeammateCard's are: a
    string parameter bound as Foo="this.bar" compiles cleanly and silently passes the literal text
    instead of a field's value (see TeammatesRazorSourceTests), and a non-string parameter cannot be
    mis-bound that way at all. PromptEdit itself carries the one string value this panel does hand
    back (the edited text), wrapped so the Razor attribute binds a record instance rather than a bare
    string.

    Stage 3 (the MudBlazor migration) converts this panel's controls per docs/engineering's rules and
    the migration brief's Part A mapping: the textarea becomes a MudTextField (with the old
    ".teammate-card-hint" helper span folded into its HelperText), the three status spans become
    MudChip, the issue list becomes one MudAlert per issue, the section wrapper becomes a MudPaper,
    and the Reset button becomes a secondary MudButton. The field wrapper, its header row, the field
    label and the placeholder list are left exactly as they were - Part A does not name them, and
    changing them would be inventing a conversion the brief did not ask for.
*@

@using Agency.Huddle.App.Prompts

@foreach (var group in this.Groups)
{
    <MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-4">
        <h2 class="prompts-group-heading">@group.Label</h2>

        @foreach (var field in group.Fields)
        {
            <div class="prompts-field">
                <div class="prompts-field-header">
                    <span class="prompts-field-label">@field.Label</span>
                    @if (field.Timing == PromptTiming.NextSession)
                    {
                        <MudChip T="string" Size="Size.Small" title="Applies to teammates started after the change">Next session</MudChip>
                    }
                    @if (field.IsModified)
                    {
                        <MudChip T="string" Size="Size.Small" Color="Color.Warning">Modified</MudChip>
                    }
                    @if (field.HasUnsavedChange)
                    {
                        <MudChip T="string" Size="Size.Small" Color="Color.Info">Unsaved</MudChip>
                    }
                </div>

                <MudTextField T="string"
                              Value="@field.Value"
                              ValueChanged="@(text => this.OnFieldInput(field.Key, text))"
                              Lines="@PromptFieldFactory.RowsFor(field.Value)"
                              HelperText="@field.HelperText"
                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                              Immediate="true" />

                @if (field.Placeholders.Count > 0)
                {
                    <p class="prompts-field-placeholders">
                        Placeholders:
                        @foreach (var placeholder in field.Placeholders)
                        {
                            <code class="prompts-field-placeholder">@placeholder</code>
                        }
                    </p>
                }

                @if (field.Issues.Count > 0)
                {
                    @foreach (var issue in field.Issues)
                    {
                        <MudAlert Severity="@(issue.Severity == PromptIssueSeverity.Error ? Severity.Error : Severity.Warning)" Dense="true" Class="mb-1">@issue.Message</MudAlert>
                    }
                }

                <div class="prompts-field-actions">
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                               Disabled="@(!field.IsModified)"
                               OnClick="@(() => this.OnResetClicked(field.Key))">Reset</MudButton>
                </div>
            </div>
        }
    </MudPaper>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Every prompt field to render, already grouped and ordered by <see cref="PromptFieldFactory"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<PromptFieldGroup> Groups { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>Raised whenever a field's value changes, carrying the edited key and its new pending text.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<PromptEdit> ValueChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised when a field's Reset button is clicked, carrying that field's key.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> ResetRequested { get; set; }

    private Task OnFieldInput(string key, string? text)
    {
        return this.ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(new PromptEdit(key, text ?? string.Empty));
    }

    private Task OnResetClicked(string key)
    {
        return this.ResetRequested.InvokeAsync(key);
    }
}
